   "type": "text",
   "html": "Other apparatus normally found in a school laboratory is also available. Plan an experiment to investigate the change in resistance of the lamp filament when the current in the lamp is increased. Resistance <i>R</i> is given by the equation <i>R</i> = \\(\\frac{<i>V</i>}{<i>I</i>}\\), where <i>V</i> is the potential difference (p.d.) across the lamp and <i>I</i> is the current in the lamp. You are <b>not</b> required to do this investigation. You should:",
